      "published": "",
      "collected": "2026-06-03",
      "abstract": "As the Internet becomes the main platform for global information and knowledge sharing, Large Language Models (LLMs) are widely used in Internet-based systems. However, the rapid flow of new information on the Internet challenges the timeliness, accuracy, and reliability of LLMs’ responses. Although retraining an LLM from scratch is the most direct way to update its internal knowledge, such an approach is often prohibitively expensive and impractical in reality, as it requires massive computational resources, lengthy data processing cycles, and substantial financial costs. To address this, researchers propose a more efficient alternative — Knowledge Editing (KE). This method aims to precisely modify or augment specific knowledge within LLMs without full retraining, thereby maintaining the model’s knowledge timeliness and correctness in a lightweight manner. However, our experiments show that existing knowledge editing methods struggle to handle the Bidirectional Multi-hop Expansion problem in knowledge editing. To address this limitation, this paper formally introduces the task of Bidirectional Multi-hop Knowledge Editing for LLMs, aiming to resolve the inconsistency problem that arises in traditional knowledge editing under complex relational dependencies. Furthermore, we construct a comprehensive evaluation framework, BidirectionalCounterfact, to systematically assess models’ consistency and generalization performance in bidirectional multi-hop expansion scenarios. In addition, we propose a novel knowledge editing framework, Bidirectional-Edit, which incorporates an auxiliary knowledge graph network and a reinforcement learning–based graph reasoning agent. By leveraging the structural constraints of the knowledge graph, Bidirectional-Edit effectively ensures the consistency and correctness of multi-hop relational expansion after editing. Experimental results demonstrate that Bidirectional-Edit significantly outperforms existing baseline methods across multiple datasets and exhibits stronger generalization ability and more robust knowledge propagation performance.",
      "abstract_zh": "互联网信息快速更新对大语言模型知识时效性提出要求，全量重训成本过高，知识编辑可轻量修改特定知识，但现有方法难以处理双向多跳扩展问题。本文提出双向多跳知识编辑任务，构建BidirectionalCounterfact评测框架，提出结合知识图与强化学习推理agent的Bidirectional-Edit方法，实验证明其性能优于现有基线。",
