      "direction_name": "模型遗忘与安全干预",
      "week": "2026-W23",
      "title": "Unlearning Isn't Deletion: Investigating Reversibility of Machine Unlearning in LLMs",
      "title_zh": "遗忘并非删除：探究大语言模型中机器遗忘的可逆性",
      "authors": [
        "Xiaoyu Xu",
        "Xiang Yue",
        "Yang Liu",
        "Qingqing Ye",
        "Huadi Zheng",
        "Peizhao Hu",
        "Minxin Du",
        "Haibo Hu"
      ],
      "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2505.16831v3",
      "pdf_url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2505.16831v3",
      "category": "cs.CL",
      "published": "2025-05-22 16:02:10+00:00",
      "collected": "2026-06-05",
      "abstract": "Unlearning in large language models (LLMs) aims to remove specified data, but its efficacy is typically assessed with task-level metrics like accuracy and perplexity. We show that these metrics can be misleading, as models can appear to forget while their original behavior is easily restored through minimal fine-tuning. This \\emph{reversibility} suggests that information is merely suppressed, not genuinely erased. To address this critical evaluation gap, we introduce a \\emph{representation-level analysis framework}. Our toolkit comprises PCA similarity and shift, centered kernel alignment (CKA), and Fisher information, complemented by a summary metric, the mean PCA distance, to measure representational drift. Applying this framework across multiple unlearning methods, data domains, and LLMs, we identify four distinct forgetting regimes based on their \\emph{reversibility} and \\emph{catastrophicity}. We compare recovery strategies and show that relearning efficiency relies on the data source. We also find that irreversible, non-catastrophic forgetting is exceptionally challenging. By probing unlearning limits, we identify a case of seemingly irreversible, targeted forgetting, offering insights for more robust erasure algorithms. Overall, our findings expose a gap in current evaluation and establish a representation-level foundation for trustworthy unlearning.",
      "abstract_zh": "大语言模型遗忘旨在移除指定数据，现有评估常采用准确率、困惑度等任务级指标。本文指出这类指标存在误导性，模型看似遗忘仅需少量微调即可恢复原行为，说明信息仅被抑制而非真正删除。本文提出表征层分析框架，结合多种指标识别出四类基于可逆性与灾难性的遗忘机制，为可信遗忘建立了表征层评估基础。",
      "has_code": false,
      "repo_url": "",
      "repo_stars": 0,
      "hf_upvotes": 0,
      "citation_count": 0,
      "venue": "ICML",
