      "id": "2606.08274",
      "direction_id": "multi-agent-consistency",
      "direction_name": "多 Agent 交互与一致性",
      "week": "2026-W24",
      "title": "Toward Human-Centered Multi-Agent Systems: Integrating Cognition, Culture, Values, and Cooperation in AI Agents",
      "title_zh": "迈向以人为本的多智能体系统：在AI智能体中整合认知、文化、价值观与协作",
      "authors": [
        "Safia Baloch",
        "Rahemeen Khan"
      ],
      "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2606.08274v1",
      "pdf_url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2606.08274v1",
      "category": "cs.MA",
      "published": "2026-06-06 17:40:21+00:00",
      "collected": "2026-06-09",
      "abstract": "The emergence of large language model (LLM)-based agents and multi-agent systems has enabled a shift from narrow task automation to more autonomous decision-making. Despite progress in language generation, planning, tool use, and coordination, most agents still treat intelligence as prediction, optimization, and task completion. Human environments are social and normative, where people reason under bounded rationality, communicate in culturally situated language, and make decisions guided by values, beliefs, trust, and social norms. This survey argues that future AI agents, especially those acting on behalf of humans, must move beyond task competence toward human-centered capabilities.   We review research across six areas: (1) evolution of intelligent agents, (2) human cognition and decision-making, (3) language, culture, and social context, (4) human values and belief systems, (5) human-agent collaboration, and (6) multi-agent coordination and modeling of human characteristics. We synthesize work from cognitive science, sociolinguistics, computational social science, and AI alignment, along with recent advances in LLM agents, cultural alignment benchmarks, preference learning, explainability, and agent societies. We identify a key gap: existing systems do not provide a unified framework integrating cognition, culture, values, and social behavior into autonomous agents. We conclude with directions for building culturally aware, value-aligned, cognitively grounded, and cooperative multi-agent systems.",
      "abstract_zh": "基于大语言模型的智能体与多智能体系统推动AI从狭窄任务自动化转向更自主的决策。现有进展虽覆盖生成、规划、工具使用与协调，但多数智能体仍将智能视为预测、优化与任务完成，忽略人类环境的社会规范性。本文作为综述梳理六大领域研究，指出现有系统缺乏整合认知、文化、价值观与社会行为的统一框架，提出未来研究方向。",
